": 0.10108864696734059}, {"text": "Michael is in training for a local marathon. He is training by completing practice runs", "x0": 0.13406593406593406, "y0": 0.13919129082426127, "x1": 0.8098901098901099, "y1": 0.15241057542768274}, {"text": "a)", "x0": 0.07032967032967033, "y0": 0.13996889580093314, "x1": 0.08461538461538462, "y1": 0.15163297045101087}, {"text": "over the marathon course. So far he has completed three practice runs with times", "x0": 0.13186813186813187, "y0": 0.15707620528771385, "x1": 0.7934065934065934, "y1": 0.16951788491446346}, {"text": "shown below.", "x0": 0.13296703296703297, "y0": 0.17418351477449456, "x1": 0.23736263736263735, "y1": 0.18429237947122862}, {"text": "{ Week 1 | Week 2 Week 3", "x0": 0.1813186813186813, "y0": 0.20295489891135304, "x1": 0.5098901098901099, "y1": 0.22706065318818042}, {"text": "3 hours | 2 hours 51 minutes | 2 hours 42 minutes 27 seconds", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.22006220839813376, "x1": 0.6912087912087912, "y1": 0.24494556765163297}, {"text": "i) Show that these times form a geometric series with a common ratio r = 0.95", "x0": 0.13186813186813187, "y0": 0.27916018662519443, "x1": 0.810989010989011, "y1": 0.291601866251944}, {"text": "(a)", "x0": 0.7538461538461538, "y0": 0.29704510108864696, "x1": 0.7725274725274726, "y1": 0.30870917573872475}, {"text": "ii) If this series continues, what would be his expected time in Week 5, to the", "x0": 0.13186813186813187, "y0": 0.33048211508553654, "x1": 0.7901098901098901, "y1": 0.3429237947122862}, {"text": "nearest second? (1)", "x0": 0.19230769230769232, "y0": 0.3475894245723173, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.359253499222395}, {"text": "iii) many hours, minutes and seconds (to the nearest second) will he have", "x0": 0.13186813186813187, "y0": 0.3810264385692068, "x1": 0.798901098901099, "y1": 0.39346811819595645}, {"text": "run in total in his practice runs in these 5 weeks? (1)", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.39813374805598756, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.4105754276827372}, {"text": "iv) If the previous winning time for the marathon was 2 hours and 6 minutes,", "x0": 0.13076923076923078, "y0": 0.43157076205287714, "x1": 0.7835164835164835, "y1": 0.4440124416796267}, {"text": "how many weeks must he keep practising to be able to run the marathon", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.44867807153965783, "x1": 0.7813186813186813, "y1": 0.46111975116640747}, {"text": "in", "x0": 0.7879120879120879, "y0": 0.4494556765163297, "x1": 0.8, "y1": 0.45878693623639194}, {"text": "less than the previous winning time? (2)", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.46267496111975115, "x1": 0.7714285714285715, "y1": 0.4821150855365474}, {"text": "b)", "x0": 0.06923076923076923, "y0": 0.5, "x1": 0.08241758241758242, "y1": 0.5116640746500778}, {"text": "A rectangular beam of width w cm and depth, d cm is cut from a cylindrical pine log", "x0": 0.12857142857142856, "y0": 0.6500777604976672, "x1": 0.8, "y1": 0.6625194401244168}, {"text": "as shown", "x0": 0.12857142857142856, "y0": 0.6671850699844479, "x1": 0.2010989010989011, "y1": 0.6765163297045101}, {"text": "The diameter of the cross section of the log (and hence the diagonal of the cross", "x0": 0.12857142857142856, "y0": 0.6765163297045101, "x1": 0.7758241758241758, "y1": 0.7013996889580093}, {"text": "section of the beam) is 15cm.", "x0": 0.12857142857142856, "y0": 0.7006220839813375, "x1": 0.36043956043956044, "y1": 0.7130637636080871}, {"text": "The strength S of the beam is proportional to the product of its width and the square", "x0": 0.12747252747252746, "y0": 0.7177293934681181, "x1": 0.810989010989011, "y1": 0.7301710730948678}, {"text": "of its depth, so that", "x0": 0.12857142857142856, "y0": 0.7348367029548989, "x1": 0.2846153846153846, "y1": 0.7465007776049767}, {"text": "w", "x0": 0.27692307692307694, "y0": 0.7636080870917574, "x1": 0.2923076923076923, "y1": 0.7884914463452566}], [{"text": "Question 4 (continued)", "x0": 0.10989010989010989, "y0": 0.07542768